|| 3.11.14 ||

saṃvatsaraḥ parivatsara iḍāvatsara eva ca |

 anuvatsaro vatsaraś ca viduraivaṃ prabhāṣyate ||

madhvaḥ : iḍāvatsaranāmāsau nakṣatradvādaśasthitaḥ |

tithīnāṃ dvādaśāvarte yo hariḥ so'nuvatsaraḥ ||

vatsaro yaḥ sthitas tv ahnāṃ ṣaṣṭyuttaraśatatraye |

gurvāvarte dvādaśāṃśe yaḥ sthaḥ sa parivatsaraḥ ||

sauradvādaśake māse yaḥ sthaḥ saṃvatsaro hariḥ |

evaṃ sa kālanāmāpi kālasthaḥ parameśvaraḥ || iti brahmatarke |

sarvadā darśanāt tasyānimiṣatvaṃ vidur budhāḥ |

satataṃ gamanād vāpi kālasthasya mahātmanaḥ || iti ca ||14||

śrīdharaḥ : saṃvatsarādibhedaś ca
saurabārhaspatyasāvanacāndranākṣatramāsabhedena draṣṭavyaḥ | kecit
punar evam āhuḥ | yadā śuklapakṣapratipadi saṅkrāntir bhavati
sauracāndramāsayor yugapad upakramo bhavati sa saṃvatsaraḥ | tataḥ
sauramānena varṣe ṣaṭ dināni vardhante cāndramānena varṣe ṣaṭ dināni
hrasantīti dvādaśadinavyavadhānād ubhayor agrapaścād bhāvo bhavati |
evaṃ vyavadhānatāratamyena pañcavarṣāṇi gacchanti | tanmadhye dvau
malamāsau bhavataḥ | punaḥ ṣaṣṭhaḥ saṃvatsaro bhavati ||14||

kramasandarbhaḥ : na vyākhyātam.

viśvanāthaḥ : graharkṣatārācakrastha ity uktam, ataḥ sūryagatyā
